LinkPulse database migrations
============================

The application never creates or updates the schema on startup. Apply migrations
explicitly before serving requests. Alembic uses DATABASE_URL from app.database,
including its local PostgreSQL default, and loads all tables from app.models.

With application dependencies installed and PostgreSQL running:

    export DATABASE_URL='postgresql+psycopg://linkpulse:linkpulse@localhost:5432/linkpulse'
    alembic upgrade head
    alembic current

For an isolated SQLite database:

    DATABASE_URL=sqlite+pysqlite:////tmp/linkpulse.db alembic upgrade head

To generate future migrations after changing models:

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the schema change"

Review generated migrations before applying them. Check schema drift with:

    alembic check

The initial migration creates links and its unique short_code index. clicks and
created_at retain their SQLAlchemy Python defaults; no server defaults are added.

On a disposable database, undo the initial migration with:

    alembic downgrade base

This drops links and its data. For an existing database created by the old
application, verify that its schema exactly matches revision 0001 before using
`alembic stamp 0001` to record that baseline without recreating tables. Stamping
only records the version; it does not validate or modify the existing schema.
